# 03 · MDA-1 micro-architecture

MDA-1 ("MoE Decode ASIC") is a **proposed, simulated** design. Nothing here is silicon. Every
quantitative property below is a simulator output (`configs/hw/asic_mda1.yaml`,
`results/decode.json`) or the RTL testbench (`rtl/`). One MDA-1 "chip" is a **package of two dies**,
each with four HBM3E stacks, like a B300.

## 1. System

A decode group is 4 MDA-1 packages on one board, fully meshed. A GPU prefill pool hands over KV via
RDMA: 890 B/token of global KV plus a 128-row SWA replay.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph PF["GPU prefill pool (unchanged)"]
    G1[GB300 / B300] --- G2[...]
  end
  subgraph DG["MDA-1 decode group (one board)"]
    direction TB
    A0["MDA-1 #0<br/>2 dies, 8x HBM3E, 8 TB/s"] <-->|"300 GB/s/dir"| A1["MDA-1 #1"]
    A0 <--> A2["MDA-1 #2"]
    A0 <--> A3["MDA-1 #3"]
    A1 <--> A2
    A1 <--> A3
    A2 <--> A3
    L0[(LPDDR5X<br/>Engram shard)] --- A0
    L1[(LPDDR5X)] --- A1
    L2[(LPDDR5X)] --- A2
    L3[(LPDDR5X)] --- A3
  end
  H["Host: tokenizer, sampler params,<br/>KV directory (Redis), RDMA"] --- DG
  PF -- "global KV 890 B/token<br/>+ encoder tail (RDMA)" --> DG
```

Partitioning is the engine's TP4 layout: heads, `wo` groups, experts by intermediate dim. We store
experts unpadded. A layer has 2 all-reduces of 6 x 5,120 BF16. More than 4 packages would need a
switched fabric, which is not designed here. Sharding the projections the GPU engine replicates
(`DecodeWorkload.shard_replicated`) *loses* on MDA-1: {{ D.ablation.shard_replicated_on_mda1.tok_s_user|n }}
vs {{ C.asic.tok_s_user|n }} tok/s/user. The extra collectives cost more than the 0.8 GB of replicated
reads they save.

## 2. Package and die

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph PKG["MDA-1 package (2.5D, CoWoS-L class)"]
    direction LR
